 "sessionCode": "PR1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/23/2023", "sessionEndDt": "05/20/2023", "sessionLong": "Project Session Full", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "Members of the ECP occasionally give independent (also called \"directed\") studies in engineering communications, typically with students who are ready for advanced work in technical communication. A student doing a directed study works one-on-one with an ECP instructor to pursue an aspect of professional communications in more depth than is possible in the ECP's regular courses. Various types of projects are possible, e.g., studying forms of technical documentation, creating user manuals, analyzing and producing technical visuals, reading and writing about problems in engineering performance, and communicating about technical topics for the public.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "Satisfies the College of Engineering's engineering communication requirement.", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "EN", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2839, "crseId": 355624, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ENGRC", "catalogNbr": "3350", "titleShort": "Organizational Comm for Eng", "titleLong": "Organizational Communications for Engineers", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 9041, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "02:45PM", "timeEnd": "04:00PM", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/09/2023", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "rae27", "firstName": "Rick", "middleName": "", "l